            <div xml:id="d452">

                <pb facs="0517" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Marseille</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-13T18:00:00-05:00">April 13, 1937—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 12th, 4 p.m. Endeavor ascertain whether 15 men enter Spain after
                    release.</p>
                <p>Department desires return passports to Consulate for disposition as set forth
                    Department’s 162 April 7 to Embassy. Furnish details Embassy so matter can be
                    taken up with Minister Justice.</p>
                <p>Department does not desire that representative be sent for scheduled trials
                    Perpignan. However, keep in touch with cases and advise Department
                    developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
